I have implemented the `clamp` function to return the `low` value if the input is below the range, the `high` value if it is above, and the original value if it is within the range. I also added comprehensive tests in `clamp.test.mjs` to cover all three execution branches.

```javascript
// clamp.mjs
export function clamp(value, low, high) {
  if (value < low) return low;
  if (value > high) return high;
  return value;
}
```

The tests verify the following:
- Value inside range: `clamp(5, 0, 10)` returns `5`.
- Value below range: `clamp(-5, 0, 10)` returns `0`.
- Value above range: `clamp(15, 0, 10)` returns `10`.
